.TH SURFCTL 1 "October 2026" "surfd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
surfctl \- change the surfd desktop from one TOML file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B surfctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B surfctl
edits
.I ~/.config/surfd/surfd.toml
(keeping comments), regenerates the Sway, Waybar, mako, fuzzel, foot,
swaylock, GTK and Qt configuration, and applies it to the running session.
A generated Sway configuration that fails validation is never written.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B theme list | set NAME [--variant dark|light] | variant toggle
List or switch theme packs.
.TP
.B theme install PATH | export NAME [DIR] | new NAME [--from BASE]
Install a theme folder or archive, share one, or start a new one.
.TP
.B accent #RRGGBB | reset
Set the accent colour.
.TP
.B wallpaper set FILE [--mode fill|fit|center|tile|stretch] | reset | list | status
Use your own image, go back to the default wallpaper, list what is installed, or show what is on screen.
.TP
.B wallpaper dynamic NAME|off | sync auto|theme|frame [FRAME] | location LAT LON|auto
Dynamic wallpapers change through the day. Pick a set, choose what it follows (the time of day, the
light/dark style, or one fixed frame) and, for sets that follow the sun, say where you are.
.TP
.B bar layout left=A,B center=C right=D,E | preset NAME | position top|bottom
Arrange the bar. Run
.B surfctl bar modules
for module names.
.TP
.B keys list | actions | bind COMBO ACTION... | unbind COMBO
Manage key bindings, e.g.
.B surfctl keys bind Mod+F1 exec foot -e htop
.TP
.B set KEY VALUE / get KEY / explain [PREFIX]
Change, read or describe any setting.
.TP
.B reload
Regenerate everything and apply it live.
.TP
.B reset [SECTION] [--yes]
Reset everything, or one section, to the defaults. A backup is kept;
.B surfctl backups restore latest
undoes it.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the configuration, themes and required programs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/surfd/surfd.toml
Your configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/surfd/defaults/surfd.toml
The defaults every missing key falls back to.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/surfd/themes/
Your theme packs (override system ones with the same name).
.TP
.I ~/.config/surfd/sway.d/*.conf
Raw Sway configuration appended to the generated one.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/surfd/
Generated files, backups and the session log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR surfd-session (1),
.BR surfd-hwprobe (1),
.BR sway (5)
